      "side": 1,
      "message": "Apologies for commenting on the commit message...\n\nFeel free to read go/commit for a few \"practices\" of how to word commit messages. \n\nTwo main points:\n\n1. as a recommendation, the first line of the commit should be imperative (Add testOnly attribute vs Adding testOnly attribute)\n\n2. when possible, for the \"Test:\" lines, you can provide a command to run the test. E.g. \"Test: atest MyUnittestClass\". Sometimes that\u0027s not possible but given there are unit tests that were modified here, we can at least run them. Also, for unittests under soong, saying \"Test: m nothing\" is enough because that runs the unit tests.",
      "revId": "30c71f119e4d452e283ce4d95c923f4ececd4f09",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
